course: dictionary
lesson: 6980
title: Clues in the body: panting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Panting means breathing fast and loudly with your mouth open. You pant after running hard, or when you are very hot. The words around the word give you the clues: fast, loud and open mouth.
explain: «She arrived panting.» The word arrived tells you she had come somewhere, and panting shows she was out of breath. Try the swap: "She arrived breathing fast and loudly." It still makes sense, so panting means that.
explain: The entry also gives an older meaning: panting for something means wanting it very much. This use is old-fashioned, so look for clues. «Young apes make a panting laugh when tickled or play-wrestling, which shows it is only a game.» Here the clues are tickled and play-wrestling, so the laugh is a fast, breathy, playful sound, not a sad one.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Panting» means breathing fast and loudly with your mouth open.
fact: You often pant after running, or when you are very hot.
fact: Dogs pant to cool down because they cannot sweat much.
fact: «Panting for» something means wanting it very much; this use is old-fashioned.
exercise: «She arrived panting.» What does panting show about her? | She was very cold and shivering | *She had lost her shoes | She had just woken from a long sleep | She was out of breath after running
exercise: Why do dogs pant on a hot day? | To smell their dinner | To tell the time | To make friends with the birds | *To cool down, because they cannot sweat much
exercise: In «Young apes make a panting laugh when tickled or play-wrestling, which shows it is only a game», which words are the clue that the laugh is playful? | *when tickled or play-wrestling | make a laugh | Young apes | human laughter
test: «After the race, Sam was panting and red in the face.» What does panting mean here? | Sleeping very deeply | *Breathing fast and loudly after running | Feeling cold and wet | Singing a loud song
test: In an old story, someone is «panting for» water. What does that mean? | *Wanting water very much | Spilling the water on the floor | Pouring the water out slowly | Swimming in a river
exam: «The dog panted in the sun, its tongue hanging out.» What does panted mean? | Barked at the postman | Fell asleep in the shade | *Breathed fast and loudly, probably to cool down | Ran away from home
